<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	The CoreTend Finder Sync extension. macOS app extensions are always
	sandboxed regardless of the host, so App Sandbox is declared here
	explicitly.

	That is the ONLY entitlement. The extension:
	  * reads the current Finder selection via FIFinderSyncController
	    (the FinderSync API itself — no file entitlement needed);
	  * classifies each URL using bounded file attributes (no contents read);
	  * opens one coretend:// URL via NSWorkspace to hand a path to the
	    host (opening a URL needs no entitlement).

	Deliberately absent, because nothing here uses them:
	  * com.apple.security.files.user-selected.read-only — the extension
	    never reads file contents; the non-sandboxed host does every
	    substantive inspection / scan after the user picks an action.
	  * com.apple.security.application-groups — the handoff is a URL, not
	    a shared-container file, so no App Group is required (unlike the
	    WidgetKit extension, which does need one).
	  * network, iCloud, push, automation, privileged-helper,
	    com.apple.security.cs.* exceptions — none apply.
	-->
	<key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
